# Configuration Guide

This project has three main configuration files:

```text
.env               private Bybit keys, gateway tokens and deployment values; never commit it
docker-compose.yml starts the Bybit gateway and the qkt daemon
qkt.config.yaml    qkt runtime behavior and the Bybit gateway broker entries
```

## .env

Start with testnet:

```dotenv
QKT_IMAGE_TAG=v{{QKT_VERSION}}
BYBIT_TRADER_TOKEN=
BYBIT_GUARDIAN_TOKEN=
BYBIT_API_KEY=
BYBIT_API_SECRET=
BYBIT_ENVIRONMENT=testnet
BYBIT_TRADE_MODE=demo
BYBIT_ACCOUNT_LOGIN=
```

- `BYBIT_API_KEY` and `BYBIT_API_SECRET` come from Bybit and go only to the gateway. Use a
  restricted key (no withdrawal) and testnet first.
- `BYBIT_TRADER_TOKEN` and `BYBIT_GUARDIAN_TOKEN` are any long random strings
  (`openssl rand -hex 32`). qkt sends the trader token to the gateway; guardrails sends the
  guardian token to reach the kill switch.
- `BYBIT_ENVIRONMENT` is `testnet` or `mainnet` (real money). The gateway refuses to start
  without it.
- `BYBIT_TRADE_MODE` and `BYBIT_ACCOUNT_LOGIN` are what qkt expects the gateway to report
  (`demo` on testnet, `real` on mainnet). qkt refuses to start when they disagree.

Optional alerts:

```dotenv
TELEGRAM_ENABLED=false
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=
```

## docker-compose.yml

Compose starts `gateway-bybit-linear` (the qkt-venue-gateway with `GATEWAY_ADAPTER=bybit`
and `GATEWAY_SETTING_CATEGORY=linear`) and the `qkt` service, which waits for the gateway to
be healthy. `gateway-bybit-spot` is the same for spot, started with
`docker compose --profile spot up -d`. Each gateway keeps its journal in its own volume and is
published on `127.0.0.1` (ports 8444 and 8445) for `curl` and the kill switch.

The gateway image is built once from
[github.com/elitekaycy/qkt-venue-gateway](https://github.com/elitekaycy/qkt-venue-gateway)
unless `GATEWAY_IMAGE` names one you already have. Its Bybit settings are listed on the
adapter's page:
https://github.com/elitekaycy/qkt-venue-gateway/blob/main/adapter-bybit/README.md

## qkt.config.yaml

Each entry under `brokers:` is one trading account, and its name is the prefix strategies
use: `bybit_linear` serves `BYBIT_LINEAR:` symbols and `bybit_spot` serves `BYBIT_SPOT:`
symbols. Both are `type: gateway` entries pointing at their gateway service. Delete an entry
you don't trade, and uncomment `bybit_spot` once its gateway runs. qkt checks each gateway's
adapter, account and trade mode at startup and refuses to start on a mismatch.

Keep risk limits explicit before using real funds. Testnet passing is not proof
that a strategy is safe for live money.

## State

qkt writes runtime state under `./state`, and each gateway its journal in its own volume.
Keep both when you care about deployed strategy state, reconciliation, or restart recovery.
